// PublicGetInstruments performs a GET /public/get_instruments (the `PublicGetInstruments` operationId) request.
//
// Retrieves trading instruments, filtered by `currency` and optional `kind`. Responses are cached for about 1 minute and can be stale relative to live book state.
//
// **Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. To avoid rate limits, Deribit recommends using either the REST requests for server-cached data or the WebSocket subscription to [instrument_state.{kind}.{currency}](https://docs.deribit.com/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentstatekindcurrency) for real-time updates. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).
//
// With `expired=false` (default) the list is not limited to tradable books. It includes visible instruments (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, `halted`) plus inactive non-combo instruments. Inactive combos are omitted; combo kinds (`future_combo`, `option_combo`) return only visible books. `is_active` can therefore be `false` on this default list. Only `state` `open` accepts new orders.
//
// With `expired=true` the list is instruments still in the live table with `state` `delivered` , recently expired, not archivized. Older expired or archivized names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.
//
// `currency` matches derivatives by settlement currency: inverse (reversed) contracts settle in the base coin (`BTC` for BTC-PERPETUAL), linear contracts typically settle in the quote coin (`USDC` for BTC_USDC-PERPETUAL). `currency=any` returns every settlement currency.
//
// Spot matching is different. A spot's settlement field is the pair symbol (for example `BTC_USDC`), not `BTC` or `USDC`. When `expired=false` and `kind` is omitted/`any` for a specific currency, the response unions (1) derivatives with that settlement currency and (2) spots whose base or quote is that currency. `kind=spot` with a specific currency matches spots on either side of the pair. `expired=true` does not apply that extra spot union, so recently delivered spots are not returned under `currency=BTC`.
//
// Results are sorted with perpetuals first, then by expiration. Each instrument includes `underlying_type`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange includes `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr`. Set `extended=true` for extra commission and (on futures) margin/perpetual fields that `public/get_instrument` does not return.
//
// **📖 Related Articles:**
// - [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)
// - [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)
// - [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)
