// Spot instruments omit `settlement_currency` and `settlement_period`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange also omit block-trade fields and include `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr` (present only when `true`). Futures include `max_leverage` and `max_non_default_leverage`. Some USDC spot pairs that support margin loans also include `max_leverage`. Perpetuals still have `expiration_timestamp`.
//
// **📖 Related Article:** [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)
//
// [Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instrument)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) PublicGetInstrumentWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *PublicGetInstrumentParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*PublicGetInstrumentResponse3, error) {
	rsp, err := c.PublicGetInstrument(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParsePublicGetInstrumentResponse3(rsp)
}

// PublicGetInstrumentsWithResponse performs a GET /public/get_instruments (the `PublicGetInstruments` operationId) request.
//
// Retrieves trading instruments, filtered by `currency` and optional `kind`. Responses are cached for about 1 minute and can be stale relative to live book state.
//
// **Note - This method has distinct API rate limiting requirements:** Sustained rate: 1 request/second. To avoid rate limits, Deribit recommends using either the REST requests for server-cached data or the WebSocket subscription to [instrument_state.{kind}.{currency}](https://docs.deribit.com/subscriptions/market-data/instrumentstatekindcurrency) for real-time updates. For more information, see [Rate Limits](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/rate-limits).
//
// With `expired=false` (default) the list is not limited to tradable books. It includes visible instruments (`open`, `settlement`, `locked`, `halted`) plus inactive non-combo instruments. Inactive combos are omitted; combo kinds (`future_combo`, `option_combo`) return only visible books. `is_active` can therefore be `false` on this default list. Only `state` `open` accepts new orders.
//
// With `expired=true` the list is instruments still in the live table with `state` `delivered` , recently expired, not archivized. Older expired or archivized names are looked up with `public/get_instrument`, not this method.
//
// `currency` matches derivatives by settlement currency: inverse (reversed) contracts settle in the base coin (`BTC` for BTC-PERPETUAL), linear contracts typically settle in the quote coin (`USDC` for BTC_USDC-PERPETUAL). `currency=any` returns every settlement currency.
//
// Spot matching is different. A spot's settlement field is the pair symbol (for example `BTC_USDC`), not `BTC` or `USDC`. When `expired=false` and `kind` is omitted/`any` for a specific currency, the response unions (1) derivatives with that settlement currency and (2) spots whose base or quote is that currency. `kind=spot` with a specific currency matches spots on either side of the pair. `expired=true` does not apply that extra spot union, so recently delivered spots are not returned under `currency=BTC`.
//
// Results are sorted with perpetuals first, then by expiration. Each instrument includes `underlying_type`. Spot routed to Coinbase Exchange includes `is_cbe_routed` / `is_csr`. Set `extended=true` for extra commission and (on futures) margin/perpetual fields that `public/get_instrument` does not return.
//
// **📖 Related Articles:**
// - [Using the currency Parameter](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/currency-parameter)
// - [Spot Trading: Deribit and Coinbase-Routed Instruments](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/spot-trading-venues)
// - [Options Data Collection Best Practices](https://docs.deribit.com/articles/options-data-collection-best-practices)
//
// [Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_instruments)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) PublicGetInstrumentsWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *PublicGetInstrumentsParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*PublicGetInstrumentsResponse3, error) {
	rsp, err := c.PublicGetInstruments(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParsePublicGetInstrumentsResponse3(rsp)
}

// PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrencyWithResponse performs a GET /public/get_last_settlements_by_currency (the `PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrency` operationId) request.
//
// Retrieves historical settlement, delivery, and bankruptcy events from all instruments within a given currency.
//
// **Settlement vs. delivery:** Settlement is a daily event (at 08:00 UTC) for futures and perpetual positions that converts unrealized profit and loss into realized profit and loss. Option positions do not settle. Delivery is a one-time event that occurs when a futures or options contract expires , any remaining open position is closed at the delivery price. Delivery does not apply to perpetual or spot instruments. Both events take place at 08:00 UTC, which is why they are sometimes conflated.
//
// Results can be filtered by settlement type and timestamp. Use pagination parameters (`count` and `continuation`) to retrieve large settlement histories. This data is useful for analyzing historical contract settlements and understanding market events.
//
// **Note on `profit_loss` and `session_profit_loss`:** Because this is a public endpoint, these fields are **platform-wide aggregates**, not per-account values. `profit_loss` is the sum of realized P&L of all position holders at the settlement price. `session_profit_loss` is the sum of each holder's total session P&L (realized + unrealized) across all participants.
//
// [Try in API console](https://test.deribit.com/api_console?method=%2Fpublic%2Fget_last_settlements_by_currency)
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrencyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, params *PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrencyParams, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrencyResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.PublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrency(ctx, params, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParsePublicGetLastSettlementsByCurrencyResponse(rsp)
}

